[beigel-richard@cs.yale.edu (Richard Beigel) writes:]
[] I wonder if a gelatinous cube might have eaten it.  I experimented;
[] they eat other wands but they always seem to engulf wands of wishing.

i like your hunch better ... but it depends by game.  in some games
a wand of wishing can be metallic (i.e. uranium) in which case a
cube would not eat it but a rust monster, for example, might.  in
other games a wand of wishing can be so-called organic (i.e. maple)
in which case a gelatinous cube would eat it.  this is only speculation,
i'm not sure if it fully accounts for the reason(s) why a wand of
wishing sometimes doesn't appear.

there are simple solutions to this problem (don't ask!).  basically,
(1) guarantee that the wand was created and (2) guarantee that the
wand will not be affected except by the player (you know how this
is done, don't you?) ...

